{# CI/CD integration — a modal opened from the component header ⋮ menu (open-cicd window event), not a body card. #}
{% comment %}
One command, not a configurator.

This used to ask which of five CI platforms you were on, which of three SBOM
sources you had, and whether you wanted augment / enrich / save-to-file, then
render the YAML those answers produced. Every one of those questions is one the
wizard asks in the repository it is being run in, where it can look and answer
most of them itself. Asking them here meant asking someone to describe their
repository to a form.

The wizard writes the pipeline config for whichever platform it finds, so the
five tabs became one command.
{% endcomment %}
<div x-data="{ cicdOpen: false }"
     @open-cicd.window="cicdOpen = true"
     @keydown.escape.window="if (cicdOpen) cicdOpen = false">
    <div x-show="cicdOpen"
         x-cloak
         class="fixed inset-0 z-[100]"
         role="dialog"
         aria-modal="true"
         aria-label="CI/CD integration">
        <div x-show="cicdOpen"
             x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
             x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0"
             x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100"
             x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
             x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
             x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0"
             class="tw-modal-overlay"
             @click="cicdOpen = false"></div>
        <div class="tw-modal"
             x-show="cicdOpen"
             x-trap.noscroll="cicdOpen"
             x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
             x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 scale-95"
             x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 scale-100"
             x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
             x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100 scale-100"
             x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0 scale-95"
             @click.stop>
            <div class="tw-modal-content">
                <div class="tw-modal-header">
                    <h4 class="tw-modal-title flex items-center gap-2">
                        <i class="fas fa-gears text-primary"></i>CI/CD Integration
                    </h4>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="tw-modal-close"
                            @click="cicdOpen = false"
                            aria-label="Close">
                        <i class="fas fa-times" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </button>
                </div>
                <div class="tw-modal-body">
                    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-0 mb-4">
                        Run this in your repository. The wizard detects your CI platform and package
                        manager, then writes the pipeline configuration for you.
                    </p>
                    <div class="relative bg-[#1e1e1e] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                        <pre class="p-4 m-0 overflow-x-auto"><code id="ci-cd-command-{{ component.id }}" class="text-sm text-white">docker run --rm -it \
  -v "$(pwd):/github/workspace" \
  -w /github/workspace \
  ghcr.io/sbomify/sbomify-action \
  sbomify-action wizard</code></pre>
                        <div class="absolute top-2 right-2">
                            {% include "core/components/copyable_value.html.j2" with copy_from="ci-cd-command-"|add:component.id title="Copy command" hide_value=True %}
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-3 mb-0">For a manual one-off, use Upload artifact in the component menu.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
